            0.432,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.1.1 Tuning fork"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.115,
            0.89,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An instrument that is often used for experiments with sound is a tuning fork. A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "tuning fork",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a U-shaped metal bar with a stem. It is usually made of steel or aluminium. The sides of the ‘U’ are called prongs or tines (Fig. 10.4a) which are struck on a pad to make them vibrate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.193,
            0.516,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 10.2: Let us explore"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.214,
            0.635,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Take a tuning fork and a soft rubber pad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.235,
            0.556,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Hold the tuning fork by its stem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.256,
            0.89,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Strike one of the prongs of the tuning fork gently against the rubber pad (Fig. 10.4b) and bring it close to your ear. Do you hear a sound? (Take care not to strike the tuning fork against a hard surface)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.057,
            0.344,
            0.215,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.057,
                0.344,
                0.215,
                0.454
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.05,
                0.457,
                0.213,
                0.5
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.4: (b) Striking a tuning fork against a rubber pad"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.31,
            0.89,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Now, gently touch a water surface with one of the vibrating prongs of the tuning fork. Do you see waves forming on the surface of water?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.347,
            0.889,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Repeat step 3 a few times while bringing the prongs of the tuning fork near your ear in different orientations. Do you hear the sound?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.385,
            0.89,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When you bring a vibrating tuning fork near your ear you hear the sound that is produced. When the prong touches the surface of water, waves form on the surface of water, indicating that the prongs of the tuning fork are indeed vibrating (Fig. 10.4c). These observations support the idea that sound is produced by vibrating objects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.477,
            0.278,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 13,
              "bbox": [
                0.222,
                0.477,
                0.278,
                0.505
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_13.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.483,
            0.474,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.251,
            0.51,
            0.621,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Explore various ways of producing sound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.048,
            0.525,
            0.198,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.048,
                0.525,
                0.198,
                0.624
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 18,
              "bbox": [
                0.056,
                0.638,
                0.207,
                0.696
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.4: (c) A prong of vibrating tuning fork touching the surface of water"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.528,
            0.867,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Make a list of different types of musical instruments and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "identify",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " their vibrating parts which produce sound."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.219,
            0.581,
            0.286,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.219,
                0.581,
                0.286,
                0.619
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_2_image_19.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.291,
            0.589,
            0.508,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Threads of Curiosity"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.622,
            0.867,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What if your name were a tune instead of a word? In Kongthong, a village near Shillong in Meghalaya also known as the Whistling Village every person has a ‘tune name’ that can be sung or whistled. This unique tradition, called Jingrwai Iawbei, begins at birth when a mother composes a lullaby-like tune for her child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.74,
            0.565,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.2 Propagation of Sound"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.765,
            0.889,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have seen that sound is produced by vibrating objects. How does sound reach your ear from the source? Sound travels through air but does it also travel through solids and liquids?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.825,
            0.548,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 10.3: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.846,
            0.889,
            0.9
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. You and your friend stand on opposite sides of a desk in the classroom. Let your friend gently knock or scratch on the desk. Listen carefully to the sound produced with your ear in the air."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 26,
